;; Session modes (karamazov-05z0.18, after autolith's hurry-up and Simple
;; Technical English): a named overlay a run is started with — config.edn
;; :run :modes ["hurry"], or `modes` on POST /v1/runs — whose words the
;; model reads in every turn's context block. There, and not in the system
;; prompt, so turning one on does not invalidate the cached prefix.
;;
;; A mode is {:doc what it is for, :prompt the prompt role holding its
;; words}. Add one by adding a prompt and an entry; the policy save checks
;; that every :prompt names a prompt the project has.

{:modes
 {"hurry" {:doc "Get to a working result fast: the smallest change that does what was asked."
           :prompt "mode-hurry"}
  "plain" {:doc "Write for a reader whose first language is not English: Simple Technical English."
           :prompt "mode-plain"}
  "relax" {:doc "Do not cut the work short over how long the conversation has become."
           :prompt "mode-relax"}}}
